(isolates effective context); RNN/LSTM + one S4/LTU-style SSM (long-context baselines outside conv/attention); copy-last-state and analytic rollout as floor/ceiling references; H-NC-eps trained only on single-step/short-window objective (isolates operator vs training protocol). Symmetric budget: fixed d_model/depth, measured params and FLOPs/token, identical data, tokens, optimizer schedule.\\nD. Protocol: family-level train/val/test splits disjoint in initial conditions and system parameters, plus a far-extrapolation split with out-of-range parameters. Main training on L_train with teacher forcing/scheduled sampling; \\\"long-horizon finetuning\\\" is a SEPARATE arm factor (train-only vs long-finetuned) because horizon extrapolation is known to be a curriculum artifact. Beyond-L_train evaluation uses GT simulator rollout + self-consistency (detailed balance/energy/invariant drift) + ensemble statistical match. 5 seeds/arm, median as primary statistic, paired bootstrap, identical batch order across paired arms. Multi-timescale measured with fast/slow sliding windows (local smoothness, curvature, local ACF) vs global spectral/invariant metrics, plus timescale-resolved error curve per decade of steps.\\nE. Pre-registered metrics/thresholds: primary ALOHE (area under relative-error curve to failure threshold at H = 16 L_train). CONFIRMATION requires all of: H-NC beats S0 by >=30% ALOHE (paired bootstrap 95% CI excludes 0), >=80% of rollouts inside 3-sigma tube at 16 L_train, and improvement in BOTH fast and slow slices with slow-band spectral cosine >= 0.8. FALSIFIERS: S0+ ties H-NC (capacity explains it); H-C ties H-NC (non-causality not needed); H-noL ties H-NC (long conv not needed); gain only in long-finetuned cell (protocol explains it); gain only in fast slice (no multi-timescale claim).\\nF. Analysis: slices by H, by timescale window, by dynamical regime, by seed, by train-vs-finetune; paired effect sizes + bootstrap CIs, permutation tests for spectral metrics, no single-seed conclusions. Main confound = training protocol/curriculum, closed by the arm x train/finetune factorial plus H-NC-eps; secondary confounds closed by S0+ (capacity), S0-rec (context), SSM/RNN (family), dual integrators + stable solver for GT-rollout quality.\\nG. Feasibility: implementable in THIS environment with stdlib only \\u2014 exact Hyena kernel (FFT long conv + polynomial-decay modulation, or IIR decomposition) and attention on tiny models, for unit-level verification: kernel symmetry, receptive-field length, O(n log n) scaling, FFT-vs-direct equivalence, causal/non-causal mask correctness. NOT feasible here: SiT-scale or any GPU training, hence all quantitative horizon curves are predictions, not results. Design stays valid as design-only because every scientific decision (arms, thresholds, splits, statistics, confound closures) is checkable pre-run.\\n\\nASSUMPTIONS (mine, not from any source, and absent from the brief): (1) SiT = transformer over time tokens where only the time module is swapped; (2) L_train ~512-1024 steps, extreme = >=16x L_train, absolute length ~1e4-1e5 steps; (3) synthetic/simulator dynamics domain, my candidate systems; (4) conditional generation from IC/short prefix with teacher forcing available; (5) compute budget of tens of GPU-hours per arm, 5 seeds, ~9 arms x 2 training factors; (6) Hyena = gated long depthwise conv with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, symmetric non-causal kernel; (7) the numeric thresholds 30% / 3-sigma / 0.8 are my pre-registration numbers; (8) unbounded deterministic GT rollout available.\\n\\nUNKNOWNS needing your input (topics setup_4 / setup_5): exact source definition of SiT and of its original time attention (bidirectional? relative positions? depth/heads); source training horizon and evaluation length; what the source means by \\\"multiple timescales\\\" (data property or metric?); source dataset/domain and training objective (one-step vs multi-step) and whether the Hyena variant saw equal training steps; whether my design must match source-reported numbers (then thresholds get anchored to them) or may be independently pre-registered.\", \"evidence\": \"Commands run in this session (all exit 0 unless noted): ls -la /workspace and find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -> only /workspace/task.json (511 bytes). cat /workspace/task.json -> contains question/context, \\\"datasets\\\": [], \\\"documents\\\": {\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"} (string only; find / -maxdepth 5 -name track.md -> no file). python3 --version -> 3.14.4. python3 -c \\\"import numpy\\\"/\\\"import torch\\\" -> ModuleNotFoundError for both; pip list shows no numpy/torch/scipy/sklearn. Network test urllib.request.urlopen('https://pypi.org') -> URLError \\\"Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"; pip download numpy -> FileNotFoundError (cannot fetch) => dependencies unobtainable. nvidia-smi -> \\\"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\\\" (CUDA 13.1 toolkit files exist in /usr/local but no GPU driver). nproc -> 224; free -g -> ~2011 GB total RAM. find / -maxdepth 4 -iname '*hyena*' / '*sit*' -> no project code or model files; find / -xdev -maxdepth 6 -iname '*.md' outside /usr,/lib,/proc,/sys,/etc -> empty (no source documentation). No training, no data generation, no metric computation was performed; no experimental outcomes are asserted.\", \"assumptions\": [\"SiT is interpreted as a transformer over trajectory time tokens in which only the time-mixing module is replaced; the rest of the architecture is held fixed (not stated in the brief)\", \"Training horizon L_train assumed ~512-1024 steps and 'extremely long' defined as >=16x L_train (approx 1e4-1e5 steps); the brief specifies neither\", \"Evaluation domain assumed to be synthetic/simulator dynamical systems I select (oscillator+drift, chaotic pendulum, N-body); no dataset exists in the environment and none is named in the brief\", \"Generation assumed conditional on an initial condition/short prefix, with teacher forcing available during training\", \"Compute budget assumed as tens of GPU-hours per arm, 5 seeds, ~9 arms x 2 training factors; this is my sizing, not a given constraint\", \"Hyena assumed to be the gated long depthwise convolution operator (long kernel with polynomial decay + short conv + gating) with a symmetric non-causal kernel variant\", \"Success/failure thresholds (30% ALOHE gain, 3-sigma tube, 80% retention, 0.8 spectral cosine) are proposed pre-registration numbers, not source-derived values\", \"Deterministic ground-truth rollouts are assumed available at arbitrary horizon lengths for reference metrics\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the source defines SiT's original time attention as full bidirectional attention with relative positional bias, and its exact depth/width/heads \\u2014 needed to keep the anchor arm faithful\", \"Whether the source's training horizon and evaluation lengths match my assumed values, and whether it even reports multi-step (not teacher-forced) evaluation\", \"What the source operationally means by 'multiple timescales' \\u2014 dataset property, model property, or metric \\u2014 which determines whether Block B's two-timescale domain design is sufficient\", \"Whether the source trained the Hyena variant with the same objective/step count as attention, or with a longer curriculum (this changes which controls are mandatory)\", \"Whether the paper's own reported numbers exist and must be reproduced (then thresholds must be anchored to them) or whether independent pre-registration is acceptable\", \"Whether the intended modality is scalar-state trajectories or high-dimensional observations (affects whether perceptual metrics belong in the primary criteria at all)\", \"Feasibility of the stdlib-only Hyena/attention unit checks at useful sequence lengths (~1e5) within CPU-only runtime \\u2014 to be measured, not assumed\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
