{"id": "1c8f9e04-6b0d-41d2-8782-29565e07487f", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:40:33.753228", "source": "user", "parent_id": "4af652d5-3fe4-42f0-bfe5-25ef341e0a22", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"План в целом годный, беру в работу. Инвентарь принят как есть: в /workspace только task.json, зависимостей нет, сети нет, GPU нет — фиксируем как условия, а не как результат. Допущения честно помечены, unknowns тоже; раз источник не задан, остаёмся на независимой пре-регистрации — не подгоняй пороги под «цифры из бумаги», которых у нас нет, так и напиши в финале: это наши пре-регистрационные значения, а не воспроизведение.\\n\\nПеред основным текстом три прицельных правки, их хочу видеть в финальном дизайне, остальное — по твоему плану:\\n\\n1) Развилка про природу SiT-генерации — это не мелочь, это меняет метрики. SiT в исходном смысле — генеративная модель на интерполянтах (diffusion-style), а не авторегрессионная развёртка. Так что определи явно, какая из двух схем у нас основная и почему: (a) авторегрессивный/условный rollout от IC+префикса (тогда ALOHE, error-vs-step, first-exit time работают напрямую), или (b) генерация целого окна траектории как объекта (тогда «согласованность на 16×L_train» — это уже распределительное совпадение и само-согласованность инвариантов, а не RMSE-кривая). Либо сделай это факторным (arm × generation-scheme), либо выбери одну и обоснуй; но не оставляй метрики висеть между двумя схемами. Заодно реши по modality: скалярное/низкоразмерное состояние — тогда perceptual-метрику вообще убрать и из вторичных.\\n\\n2) Сократи и рассортируй рукава по обязательности. 9 рукавов × 2 фактора × 5 сидов = 90 прогонов — как дизайн ок, но раздели на MANDATORY (S0, H-NC, H-C, H-noL, S0+ params/FLOPs-matched, S0-rec, floor/ceiling) и OPTIONAL/ablation-grade (SSM/LTU, RNN, H-NC-eps как отдельный фактор). Для каждого optional напиши одной строкой, какой rival explanation он закрывает и что теряем без него. Хочу, чтобы читатель видел минимальный набор, достаточный для атрибутирования вывода именно некаузальному Hyena.\\n\\n3) По Block A: добавь явно, что «multiple timescales» у нас — свойство задачи, операционализированное через timescale-разрешённые срезы (fast window vs slow band), и что без выигрыша в slow-срезе гипотеза считается неподтверждённой независимо от fast. Это у тебя уже есть в falsifiers — подними это в определение гипотезы, а не только в раздел опровержения.\\n\\nFeasibility-часть оставляй как есть: stdlib-only unit-checks (симметрия ядра, длина рецептивного поля, FFT-vs-direct эквивалентность, корректность causal/non-causal маски, O(n log n)) — это правильный уровень проверяемости для design-only;_training-кривые_ оформляй строго как предсказания. Присылай финальный дизайн: rationale, контролы, analysis plan, feasibility, список допущений отдельным блоком.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
{"id": "3d6f3883-70ac-4521-aa27-9b61f134ce3f", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:42:20.723667", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "1c8f9e04-6b0d-41d2-8782-29565e07487f", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "The researcher approved and wants the final design (stage=result) with three edits:\n\n1. Generation-scheme fork: SiT = Scalable Interpolant Transformer (diffusion/flow-matching style, generative over whole window). Decide: factorial arm × generation scheme, or choose one. And modality decision: low-dim state → remove perceptual metric entirely.\n2. Sort arms into MANDATORY vs OPTIONAL, one-liner per optional: rival explanation closed and what's lost without it. Minimal attribution set.\n3. Block A: \"multiple timescales\" as task property operationalized via timescale-resolved slices; no slow-band gain ⇒ hypothesis not confirmed, lifted into hypothesis definition.\n\nPlus: final must state thresholds are our pre-registration values, not reproduction. Feasibility stays as is; training curves strictly as predictions.\n\nLet me decide on the generation scheme. I think the cleanest is: primary = (b) window-generative diffusion/interpolant scheme (faithful to SiT as interpolant transformer, and non-causal Hyena only makes sense in a full-window, bidirectional setting — an autoregressive rollout would arguably require causality, which conflicts with the \"non-causal\" operator claim). Actually key insight: in scheme (a) autoregressive rollout, \"non-causal\" within the window is still possible (bidirectional within window but block-autoregressive), but the \"extremely long\" claim comes from chaining. In scheme (b), length comes from either long-window generation or overlapping window composition with consistency constraints.\n\nDesign decision: primary = (b) window-generative as the main scheme, because it's the source-faithful SiT (interpolant/diffusion) formulation and it's the only one where the non-causal operator claim is coherent; BUT the metrics that answer \"extremely long consistent trajectories\" (error-vs-step, ALOHE, first-exit) require a sequential rollout. So handle: within scheme (b), long horizon is achieved by anchored-chained generation: generate window of length L_gen = 16 L_train? Hmm.\n\nBetter: make it factorial but asymmetric — the primary scheme is (b) window-generative (matched to SiT's interpolant training), and (a) AR/conditional rollout is a SECONDARY scheme (mandatory-lite? or optional) whose purpose is to check whether the result is scheme-dependent. Researcher said: \"either make it factorial (arm × generation-scheme) or choose one and justify; but don't leave metrics hanging between the two schemes.\"\n\nI'll choose: PRIMARY = (b) window-generative (full-window sampling, conditional on short prefix + IC conditioning, or unconditional distributional generation), evaluated with distributional/structural metrics + anchored rollout metrics where GT exists. And include (a) AR rollout as a MANDATORY-lite second scheme? That doubles cost. Let me think about what's defensible and lean.\n\nActually cleanest: define the estimand precisely. The hypothesis is about the operator's ability to represent long-range dynamical structure. Two failure modes are distinct: (i) representational — does the model capture slow-band structure; (ii) compositional/rollout — does error compound over iterative composition. To attribute to the non-causal operator we should measure (i) primarily in scheme (b) (single-shot window generation, no compounding from autoregression), and (ii) secondarily in scheme (a).\n\nDecision: PRIMARY scheme = (b) \"one-shot window generation\" (whole trajectory window as a generative object), because: it is the SiT-faithful interpolant formulation; it isolates the operator from autoregressive compounding (a confound that would be shared by all arms but interacts with causality); and non-causal kernel is only meaningful for a full-window object. Metrics for primary: distributional match + invariant self-consistency + per-window structural metrics, plus \"long-window coherence\" measured inside a single generated window (which is what \"extremely long\" means in this scheme: window length 16×L_train, i.e., length extrapolation of the generative model, not iterative rollout).\n\nThen \"extremely long\" needs a definition per scheme:\n- Scheme B (primary): generated window length W, trained at W_train, evaluated at W = {1,2,4,8,16} × W_train — length extrapolation of the generative model. Consistency = (1) prefix-conditioned structural agreement: generate window conditioned on a real prefix of length P, then compare the generated continuation to GT rollout from that prefix (this recovers an error-vs-step curve WITHOUT autoregressive compounding — great! It's a \"one-shot continuation\" metric); (2) distributional match over window ensembles; (3) invariant/self-consistency drift across the window; (4) slow-band spectral match.\n\nThat's elegant: conditioned one-shot continuation gives error-vs-step curves up to W-P, no chaining. Then ALOHE applies to \"ALOHE-C\" (continuation) rather than AR rollout. And scheme (a) AR rollout becomes OPTIONAL/secondary factor to test compounding.\n\nActually the researcher wants: metrics must be scheme-locked. So:\n- Scheme B (primary): metrics set MB = {continuation error curve from a real prefix (single-shot, so step-index is relative offset within the window, no compounding), ensemble distributional distance (per-window statistics: energy, stationary histogram, power spectrum in slow band), invariant drift (energy/detailed-balance), first-exit from 3σ tube inside the window, ALOHE-C}.\n- Scheme A (secondary, optional arm factor): AR rollout metrics MA = {RMSE-vs-step vs GT rollout, first-exit time, ALOHE-AR, plus drift/accumulation exponent}.\n\nAnd define the mapping of \"success\" per scheme.\n\nModality: choose low-dimensional observable state (dim 2–16). Therefore perceptual metrics removed entirely, from primary AND secondary. Only optional: in one \"physical plausibility\" control domain with a rendered observable? No — researcher says remove if low-dim. So remove entirely; state explicitly that no perceptual metric appears anywhere. Optionally mention that if a future high-dim domain is used, perceptual metric becomes relevant but is out of scope. Good.\n\nArms:\nMANDATORY (minimal attribution set):\n1. S0 — SiT + original full non-causal time attention (anchor).\n2. H-NC — SiT + non-causal Hyena (treatment under test).\n3. H-C — causal Hyena (non-causality attribution).\n4. H-noL — Hyena without long conv (gating + short conv only) (long-kernel attribution).\n5. S0+-match — attention scaled to equal params & FLOPs (capacity attribution).\n6. S0-rec — sliding-window/local attention with context = Hyena receptive field (context-length attribution).\n7. Floor: copy-last-state / constant-jump reference. Ceiling: analytic GT rollout (and GT-with-noise reference to calibrate metric noise floor).\nOPTIONAL (ablation grade, one-liner each):\n- H-NC-ε (single-step objective only): closes \"training objective, not operator\"; without it we can't rule out that multi-step curriculum is what matters. (Note researcher says treat H-NC-eps as separate factor — yes, factor objective ∈ {multi-step, single-step}, optional.)\n- S4/LTU SSM: closes \"any global linear recurrence family would do\"; without it, family-level claim (Hyena class) unsupported, but operator-level attribution unaffected.\n- LSTM/RNN: closes \"recurrence memory suffices\"; without it, no non-transformer reference point on long-horizon stability.\n- (add) H-NC-noise-aug or long-finetuned factor: \"long-finetuned\" factor is a factor, not arm.\n- (add optional) longer-context attention at matched FLOPs via linear/performer kernel: closes \"FLOPs matching forced attention into a weak config\" — good addition, optional.\n- (add optional) H-NC with symmetric kernel replaced by antisymmetric/random kernel: closes \"it's just the kernel shape/decay\"? maybe \"kernel-decay sweep (poly vs exp vs learned)\" as optional.\n- (add optional) zero-shot length-extrapolation baselines from literature (e.g., RoPE/ALiBi attention variants): closes \"long-context tricks already handle this\".\n\nCost accounting: MANDATORY = 7 arms (7th = floor/ceiling which are free, no training) × 5 seeds → ~6 trained arms × 5 seeds = 30 runs in primary scheme. With train-only vs long-finetuned factor: researcher had 9 arms × 2 factors × 5 seeds = 90. New: 6 trained mandatory arms × 5 seeds = 30 primary runs; the finetune factor applied only to a subset (S0, H-NC, H-C) = 3×5 = 15 extra; optional arms ~4×5 = 20. Total ~65, and we should state the exact grid. Let me build a clean grid table.\n\nLet me define budget more precisely and honestly (design-only): estimated per-run FLOPs. We can't measure training FLOPs here, but we can state parameter counts analytically and give a compute model. I should be careful: any numbers about compute are estimates/assumptions.\n\nAlso: pre-registration statement — thresholds are ours, not reproduction.\n\nTimescale operationalization lifted into hypothesis definition (edit 3): H1 states: \"…captures dynamics over multiple timescales\" is defined as a property of the TASK (two-timescale domain with pre-profiled scales), measured by timescale-resolved slices; a gain confined to the fast slice is H1-NOT-CONFIRMED by definition (not merely a falsifier). Write H1 as conjunction: H1 = H1-length ∧ H1-slow ∧ H1-attribution.\n\nAlso need: rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility, assumptions as separate block. And unit-check feasibility list stays.\n\nI should perhaps run a quick feasibility check on stdlib-only ops to ground feasibility claims: e.g., measure time for FFT-based long conv at n=1e5 using pure Python (cmath) vs direct conv at small n. That would substantiate the feasibility block with real observations. Also check `statistics`/`audioop`? Python 3.14 removed audioop. There's `cmath`, `array`. FFT in pure Python at n=1e5 — 1e5 * 17 ≈ 1.7M complex ops, feasible in maybe a few seconds. Let me test quickly to make feasibility claims grounded. Also test symmetry/receptive-field check trivially.\n\nLet me write a small script that: implements direct conv O(n^2) for n=4096, and iterative radix-2 FFT O(n log n) for n=131072, verifies equivalence, checks symmetry and receptive field length. That grounds the feasibility block with actual runtime numbers. Good — that's design-support work, not an experiment outcome.\n\nAlso compute parameter counts for the operator variants analytically (attention vs Hyena) — can compute with python arithmetic, that's design-support.\n\nLet's do it.\n\nCareful with pure-Python FFT recursion: iterative Cooley-Tukey. n=131072 might take ~2-5 s in Python. Let's test with timing.\n\nLet me write files in /tmp (workspace is fine too, but design-only; writing scratch in /tmp is fine — I shouldn't clutter /workspace? It's fine either way; I'll use /tmp).\n\nThen compute params: model with d_model d, depth L. Attention block: QKVO = 4d², MLP 8d² (4d inner) => 12d² + norms. Hyena block: input projection to 3d (x, v1, v2) = 3d²? plus conv kernels (3*h + d) small, output proj d² => 4d² + MLP 8d² = 12d². So matched-ish by width adjustment. Fine — state analytically.\n\nLet me run the checks.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "mkdir -p /tmp/feas && cat > /tmp/feas/ops.py <<'PY'\nimport cmath, math, time\n\ndef fft(a, inv=False):\n    n = len(a)\n    if n <= 1: return a[:]\n    even = fft(a[0::2], inv); odd = fft(a[1::2], inv)\n    T = [cmath.exp(2j*math.pi*k/n) if inv else cmath.exp(-2j*math.pi*k/n) for k in range(n//2)]\n    out = [0j]*n\n    for k in range(n//2):\n        t = T[k]*odd[k]\n        out[k] = even[k]+t; out[k+n//2] = even[k]-t\n    return out\n\ndef conv_fft(x, k):\n    n, m = len(x), len(k)\n    N = 1 << (n+m-1).bit_length()\n    X = fft(x + [0.0]*(N-n)); K = fft(k + [0.0