{"id": "95c827a8-9d8c-429d-b980-d6b15c302a90", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:47:38.225680", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "a41fcb55-47f5-4cf7-a7ad-f60231dede21", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Excellent, all checks confirm. Now write the final design (stage=result).\n\nKey content per researcher's three edits + full design. Also must state thresholds are our pre-registration values, not reproduction of paper numbers.\n\nLet me now carefully construct the final design.\n\n### Decision on generation scheme\nChoose: **Primary = (b) whole-window generative (interpolant/diffusion-style, SiT-faithful)**, with **factorial inclusion of (a) prefix-conditioned one-shot continuation** — hmm. Let me be crisp.\n\nActually, better decomposition that keeps metrics non-hanging: define THREE evaluation modes tied to one generative model, all from the SAME window-generative model (no separate AR model needed):\n\n- M1 **Single-shot window generation (unconditional/param-conditioned)**: model generates a full window of length W as one object. Metrics: distributional match (per-window statistics: energy, histogram, slow-band power spectrum), invariant/detailed-balance drift within window, structural diversity/collapse. No GT alignment possible (stochastic) → distributional only. This is where \"16×L_train length extrapolation\" is measured as a property of the generative object.\n- M2 **Prefix-conditioned one-shot continuation** (the key metric-bearing mode): condition the window model on a real prefix of length P (canvas/inpainting-style conditioning used in diffusion video/trajectory models — mask the future region, keep the GT prefix fixed at every denoising step), generate the continuation in ONE shot, then compare against GT rollout from the same IC. Because the continuation is produced in a single forward sampling pass, the error-vs-step curve contains NO autoregressive compounding → it isolates representational long-range structure. Metrics: relative-error curve vs offset, ALOHE, first-exit from 3σ tube, slow-band spectral match of the continuation, timescale-resolved error.\n- M3 **Iterative/AR rollout chaining** (secondary scheme, arm factor): use the model to advance by Δ and re-condition repeatedly to reach 16–32×L_train. Metrics: compounding exponent (fit log-error growth), first-exit time, ALOHE-AR, invariant drift.\n\nSo the fork is resolved as: **primary = (b) window-generative (SiT-faithful), with the hypothesis measured in M2 (one-shot continuation) as the primary estimand and M1 as the distributional companion; (a) AR chaining (M3) is a mandatory-lite secondary scheme applied only to the three attribution-critical arms** (S0, H-NC, H-C) — because it tests whether the conclusion survives the scheme change, and it's the scheme where the \"trajectory\" is literally generated long. Justification: (i) SiT is an interpolant/diffusion generative model, so window-object generation is the faithful instantiation; (ii) a non-causal operator is only meaningful for an object that is generated as a whole (in strict AR rollout, bidirectionality within the window collapses to a boundary effect and the \"non-causal\" claim becomes untestable); (iii) M2 gives error-vs-step curves without confounding by compounding, which M3 conflates.\n\nAlso the failure mode: M3 tests compounding, M2 tests representation; the hypothesis needs both, and we pre-register which claim each supports.\n\nModality decision: **low-dimensional observable state (d ∈ {2..16})** as primary; therefore **perceptual metrics removed entirely**, including secondary. Explicitly stated. Optional high-dim domain deferred as out-of-scope (mention that perceptual metrics would return only if modality changed, which is out of scope here).\n\nHmm — should I include a \"high-dimensional\" extension? Researcher: \"Заодно реши по modality: скалярное/низкоразмерное состояние — тогда perceptual-метрику вообще убрать и из вторичных.\" So decide low-dim, remove perceptual metrics entirely. Do that.\n\n### Arms sorted MANDATORY/OPTIONAL\nMANDATORY (7): S0, H-NC, H-C, H-noL, S0±(params/FLOPs matched), S0-rec, refs (floor: copy-last-state + white-noise/shuffled surrogate; ceiling: analytic GT rollout + GT-noise reference).\nWait researcher grouped floor/ceiling in mandatory. Keep as \"R-refs\" (no training, free).\n\nOPTIONAL (ablation-grade), each one-liner: rival explanation closed / cost of omitting:\n- O1 H-NC-ε (single-step objective only; better implemented as objective × arm factor): closes \"the multi-step/consistency objective, not the operator\"; without it, attribution to the operator is contaminated by training-objective confound.\n- O2 S4/LTU-style global SSM: closes \"any global linear-recurrence class would do — Hyena isn't special\"; without it, the claim stays operator-level, not family-level.\n- O3 LSTM/GRU: closes \"recurrent memory alone handles long horizons\"; without it, no non-attention/non-conv reference point.\n- O4 ALiBi/RoPE-scaled attention at matched FLOPs (long-context baseline): closes \"standard long-context positional tricks already give length extrapolation\"; without it, a reviewer can say we strawmanned the attention baseline.\n- O5 Hyena kernel-decay sweep (poly α ∈ {0.5,1,1.5,2} / exp / learned): closes \"an arbitrary kernel-shape sensitivity drove the gap\"; without it, effect size may be an artifact of one hyperparameter (recommend at minimum this one if compute permits).\n- O6 width/depth iso-FLOPs sweep for both families (scale-proxy): closes \"we matched at one operating point only\"; without it, capacity parity is a point estimate.\n\nMinimal attribution set (explicit): S0 vs H-NC = effect exists; H-C = it's non-causality; H-noL = it's the long kernel; S0± = not capacity; S0-rec = not raw context length; refs = metric calibration. State that if only the mandatory set runs, the claim is limited to \"non-causal long-kernel operator in this architecture/task\", and family-level claims require O2/O3.\n\n### Grid and budget\n- Primary scheme (M1+M2 from a single trained checkpoint): 6 trained mandatory arms × 5 seeds = 30 runs.\n- Long-finetune factor (train-only vs long-finetune) applied to S0, H-NC, H-C: +15 runs (3 arms × 5 seeds).\n- M3 (AR chaining): inference-only on the same checkpoints for S0, H-NC, H-C → no extra training, GPU-hours of sampling.\n- Optional: O1 objective factor (single-step) on S0, H-NC: +10; O2–O6: ~10–25 runs.\nTotal: 30 mandatory + 15 factor + 10 optional-min = 55 trained runs (vs 90 in v1). Note that the researcher's 90 = 9×2×5. I'll present 55 trained runs for the mandatory+core-factor design, plus optional.\n\nCompute sizing: state as assumptions with a formula: per-run FLOPs ≈ 6·N·D for interpolant training, with N ≈ 10–25M params (d_model 512, depth 8) and D ≈ 2–5e9 tokens for small models; on A100 (~1.5e20 FLOPs/GPU-hour at 40% MFU): ~30–130 GPU-hours per run → 55 runs ≈ 2–7k GPU-hours. This is design-only estimate, flagged as assumption, not measurable here. Also note attention O(n²) vs Hyena O(n log n) memory at W=2^14–2^17 → attention arm likely needs gradient checkpointing / flash; state as a practical constraint and require reporting wall-clock and peak memory as part of matched-budget accounting (FLOPs parity must be documented, and if attention cannot reach W=16×W_train at all, that itself is a documented, honest limitation rather than a \"win\").\n\nImportant: this is a real confound — if attention simply OOMs at extreme length, the length-extrapolation comparison at 16× is not param/FLOP matched. Handle: (i) report the max evaluable length per arm; (ii) define \"length-extrapolation frontier\" (longest length at which metric stays within threshold) as the primary length metric, since it is well-defined under differing ceilings; (iii) require the attention baseline to be also evaluated with a memory-reduced variant (sliding window/linear) at the same wall-clock, i.e., O4. Good.\n\n### Data / domain\nTwo-timescale synthetic family (pre-profiled), with explicit generation specs:\n- D1: linear stochastic oscillator with 2 well-separated eigenvalue moduli (fast decay/period ~20 steps, slow ~2000 steps) + observation noise. Ground truth = exact linear propagator (Koopman/e matrix-power) → GT rollout is exact, no integrator error → removes GT confound for the primary domain. Excellent point: primary domain should be one where GT is ANALYTIC.\n- D2: damped/driven pendulum + slow parameter drift (nonlinear, moderately chaotic; GT via two integrators).\n- D3: chaotic Lorenz/Rössler at fine step (single-timescale chaos as stress test — expected degradation everywhere; positive control for \"no operator magic\").\n- D4: N-body / lattice of coupled oscillators (spatially extended, slow coarsening) as the slow-mode-rich domain.\n- D5 (optional): real trajectory set if a small offline dataset exists (not here; network off) — marked unavailable.\nPrimary domain = D1 (analytic GT, exactly two tunable timescales τ_fast/τ_slow, ratio swept over {10, 10², 10³}) + D2 as realism check. D3 = positive control (should show no arm wins) — a design-in内置 negative control that catches metric/harness artifacts. Good.\n\nTimescale operationalization lifted into hypothesis definition.\n\n### Metrics locked per mode\nM1: per-window statistic distances (energy drift, stationary-marginal Wasserstein-1, slow-band spectral cosine, power-law/decay-time fit error), ensemble diversity, mode-collapse check.\nM2: relative error curve ê(t) normalized by GT-noise floor, ALOHE (area under ê to threshold) at W = 16 W_train, first-exit time from 3σ_GT tube, slow-band spectral cosine of continuation, τ_slow recovery error (fit exponential/oscillation decay constants), fast-window smoothness (curvature/second-difference RMS vs GT).\nM3: compounding exponent (slope of log error), ALOHE-AR, first-exit, invariant drift.\n\nPre-registration statement: thresholds are OUR numbers, not reproduction; source not available in environment.\n\nSuccess criteria (per-scheme, all required):\nC1 (existence): H-NC > S0 in M2 ALOHE by ≥30% median at W=16W_train, paired-bootstrap 95% CI excludes 0 across seeds.\nC2 (timescale): slow-slice gain: τ_slow relative recovery error improvement ≥30% AND slow-band spectral cosine ≥0.8; **fast-only gain ⇒ hypothesis NOT confirmed by definition** (part of H, not just falsifier).\nC3 (attribution): H-C worse than H-NC by ≥20% on slow-slice (else non-causality not needed); H-noL worse than H-NC by ≥20% (else long kernel not needed); |S0± − H-NC| < 10% ⇒ attributed to capacity ⇒ H1 rejected as operator claim; |S0-rec − H-NC| < 10% ⇒ attributed to context length ⇒ rejected.\nC4 (regime): D3 positive control shows no arm's advantage over floor > threshold ⇒ harness not producing artifacts... careful: for D3 we expect all arms to hit the chaos ceiling; a \"win\" there flags a leak (e.g., information from GT or leakage of test IC).\nC5 (robustness): ≥4/5 seeds individually reach the pass bar for H-NC, and effect direction consistent.\n\nFailure/partial classifications: \"supported (operator-level, representation only)\", \"supported (representation) / unsupported (compositional)\" if M3 doesn't follow, \"unsupported\" etc. Pre-register a decision table.\n\n### Analysis plan\n- primary estimand per arm: median over seeds of ALOHE / slow-slice metrics; paired by seed and IC; bootstrap 10k; Holm correction over secondary family.\n- Slices: horizon W ∈ {1,2,4,8,16,32}×W_train; timescale slices (fast window = 5τ_fast, slow band = [1/(5τ_slow), 1/τ_fast] in frequency); τ-ratio ∈ {10,100,1000}; regime (periodic/quasi/chaotic); train-only vs long-finetune.\n- Frontier analysis: max length at which slow-band cosine ≥0.8 → \"length frontier\" per arm; report as main figure.\n- Error decomposition: bias (systematic drift) vs variance vs spectral power misplacement; per-decade error curve.\n- Inter-seed repeatability: IQR/median ratio; if seed variance > effect, declare inconclusive rather than average it away.\n- Main confound: training objective/curriculum → factorial (arm × objective × finetune) + pre-registered interaction test; secondary confounds as above; GT confound closed by analytic GT in D1.\n- Power/seed sensitivity: pilot with 2 seeds on D1 to estimate σ, then fix seeds at 5 (or more) before confirmatory runs — pre-registered procedure.\n\n### Feasibility\n- design-only: nothing trained, no outcomes; all quantitative statements labeled predictions.\n- Verified here (stdlib-only, CPU): kernel symmetry exact (0.0 error), 2L−1 kernel length, FFT-vs-direct equivalence 1.3e-15/1.9e-15, pure-python FFT long conv n=65536 in 1.5 s, n=131072 in 3.2 s, direct conv n=4096/L=1024 in 0.42 s ⇒ unit checks at evaluation-relevant lengths are runnable in this environment.\n- **Critical implementation finding**: a symmetric *shape* kernel applied with right-aligned conv is still strictly causal (future-input influence on earlier outputs = 0.0); only center-aligned application is non-causal (3.5e-1). Therefore the \"non-causal\" arm must pass an influence test, not a symmetry test; boundary policy must be declared (edge truncation asymmetry observed: left-edge impulse energy 2.12 vs 0.13) — otherwise H-NC silently becomes a causal arm and the entire attribution collapses. This is the single most dangerous implementation confound; make it a blocking pre-flight test.\n- Not feasible here: training any of this, and no datasets; per-run GPU cost is an assumption-based estimate.\n\nAssumptions block, unknowns resolved-by-decision block (record researcher's rulings: independent pre-registration; low-dim modality; mandatory/optional split).\n\nAlso mention: pre-registration artifacts to produce (analysis spec file, hashes, locked metric code, unit-check log), and that predictions are stated with a table (predicted direction per arm, no numbers claimed as measured).\n\nLength: comprehensive but organized. Let's write it. Use Russian (researcher writes Russian) — the answer field in Russian, with English metric names. That's fine.\n\nBudget: also note \"arm × scheme\" factorial: I resolved as primary scheme B with M3 applied to subset — I need to justify why not full factorial: cost doubling and M3 for arms whose model can't be rolled out is uninformative; instead pre-register M3 as scheme-transfer test on 3 arms; if M3 disagrees with M2 for H-NC, we escalate to full factorial.\n\nOne more: define W_train. Assumption: W_train = 1024 steps (primary), extreme = 16× = 16384, with M3 to 32× = 32768.\n\nWrite it now.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN (design-only)\n**Question (H1):** does replacing SiT's time attention with a **non-causal Hyena** operator let the model generate extremely long, consistent trajectories that capture dynamics over **multiple timescales**?\n\n**Standing declarations.** (1) Nothing was trained; every quantitative statement below about arms is a **prediction**, never a result. (2) All thresholds are **our pre-registration values, fixed before any run — not reproduction of paper numbers**; the source paper is not present in this environment, so no anchoring to reported figures is possible. (3) Perceptual metrics are **removed entirely** (primary and secondary) — see Modality.\n\n---\n## 1. Environment facts (fixed conditions, not results)\n`/workspace` contains only `task.json` (511 B): no SiT code, no Hyena implementation/spec, no trajectory datasets (`datasets: []`), no configs, no metric code, no source text. Python 3.14 stdlib-only; numpy/torch/scipy absent; DNS dead and `pip download` fails (deps unobtainable); `nvidia-smi` cannot reach a driver (CUDA toolkit present, no driver); 224 CPUs, ~2 TB RAM. Consequence: all training-scale claims are unexecutable here; the design is validated as a design.\n\n## 2. Hypothesis, operationalized (incl. your edit 3)\n**Timescales are a property of the TASK, not of the model.** Each domain is pre-profiled (ACF decay times, eigenvalue moduli / Lyapunov exponents, power spectrum) and must expose two well-separated scales τ_fast ≈ 20–50 steps and τ_slow ≈ 10³–10⁴ steps, with ratio ρ = τ_slow/τ_fast swept over {10, 10², 10³}. Profiling is published before training; \"multi-timescale\" is then measured by **timescale-resolved slices** (fast window = 5τ_fast; slow band = frequency interval [1/(5τ_slow), 1/τ_fast]).\n\n**H1 is a conjunction, stated up front:**\n- **H1-length** — generated horizon W ≥ 16 × W_train remains consistent;\n- **H1-slow** — consistency holds in the **slow** slice (not only the fast one);\n- **H1-attrib** — the gain survives the attribution controls (causal / no-long-kernel / capacity / context-length).\n\n**A gain confined to the fast slice means H1 is NOT CONFIRMED, by definition of H1-slow** — not merely a falsifier in a later section. If H1-length holds but H1-slow fails, the verdict is pre-classified as \"short-horizon smoothing only, hypothesis unsupported.\"\n\n**Horizon:** W_train = 1024 steps (assumption); \"extremely long\" = 16× = 16 384 (assumption); chaining mode probes 32× = 32 768.\n\n## 3. Generation scheme — fork resolved (your edit 1)\nSiT in the original sense is an **interpolant/diffusion-style generative model over a whole object**, not an autoregressive unroller. We adopt **(b) whole-window generation as the primary scheme**, for three reasons: (i) it is the faithful instantiation of SiT; (ii) a **non-causal** operator is only meaningful for an object generated as a whole — under strict autoregression, bidirectionality collapses to a boundary effect and the \"non-causal\" claim becomes untestable; (iii) it lets us separate long-range **representation** from **compounding**, which a single AR curve conflates. Autoregression is retained as a **scheme-transfer test**, not as a co-primary scheme, so no metric ever \"hangs\" between schemes. One trained checkpoint serves three evaluation modes:\n\n- **M1 — single-shot window generation** (unconditional / system-parameter-conditioned). No per-step GT alignment exists (output is stochastic) → **distributional metrics only**: energy/invariant drift within the window, Wasserstein-1 distance of stationary marginals, **slow-band spectral cosine**, decay-time/τ fit error, ensemble diversity (anti-mode-collapse). Supports H1-length and H1-slow claims about the trajectory *as an object*.\n- **M2 — prefix-conditioned ONE-SHOT continuation (PRIMARY ESTIMAND).** The window model is conditioned on a real GT prefix of length P = 128 (the prefix is re-fixed at every denoising/interpolant step; the future region is generated). Because the continuation is produced in a single sampling pass, the error-vs-step curve contains **no autoregressive compounding** → it isolates representational long-range structure. Metrics: relative error ê(t) normalized by the GT-noise floor, **ALOHE** (area under ê up to failure threshold) at W = 16 W_train, first-exit time from the 3σ_GT tube, τ_slow recovery error, slow-band spectral cosine, fast-window curvature RMS.\n- **M3 — iterative/AR chaining (scheme-transfer, secondary).** The same model is re-conditioned every Δ = W_train/2 up to 32 W_train. Metrics: log-error compounding exponent (fitted slope), ALOHE-AR, first-exit, invariant drift. Applied to the three attribution-critical arms (S0, H-NC, H-C) only; if M3 contradicts M2 for H-NC, the arm × scheme factorial is escalated **as a pre-registered contingency**, not silently chosen post hoc.\n\n**Modality decision:** primary modality is **low-dimensional observable state, d ∈ {2…16}**. Therefore **no perceptual/perceptual-quality metric appears anywhere in this design** (not even as secondary); a high-dimensional/video instantiation is explicitly out of scope, and with it any perceptual metric.\n\n## 4. Data / domains\nDeterministic or exactly-solvable simulators (no network needed, no licensing, reproducible seeds).\n- **D1 (PRIMARY): linear stochastic 2-timescale oscillator** — state transition via a linear propagator with two separated eigenvalue moduli, plus observation noise. GT rollout = **exact matrix powers**, so there is **no integrator-error confound** in the primary domain; τ_fast, τ_slow, ρ, noise level are explicit knobs.\n- **D2 (realism):** damped/driven pendulum + slow parameter drift (nonlinear; GT from two independent solvers, disagreement = GT noise band).\n- **D3 (positive control, harness leak detector):** fine-step chaotic system (Lorenz/Rössler). Prediction: every arm saturates at the chaos ceiling; **a clean \"win\" here flags leakage** (GT information, IC overlap, normalization leak) and triggers harness audit.\n- **D4 (slow-mode rich):** coupled-oscillator lattice / N-body with slow coarsening — stresses the slow band.\n- **D5:** real offline trajectory corpus — **not available here** (network off, datasets empty); listed as an extension, not part of the confirmatory grid.\nSplits are **family-level**: train/val/test disjoint in initial conditions *and* in system parameters; plus a **far-extrapolation** split with parameters outside the training range.\n\n## 5. Arms, sorted by necessity (your edit 2)\nBudget parity: fixed d_model/depth family, **measured** params and FLOPs/token, identical tokens, optimizer, schedules, sampling budget; wall-clock and peak memory reported as part of the budget ledger.\n\n**MANDATORY — minimal attribution set (6 trained + 2 free references):**\n| Arm | Rival explanation it closes |\n|---|---|\n| **S0** SiT + original full (bidirectional) time attention | \"there is nothing to beat\" — anchor |\n| **H-NC** SiT + non-causal Hyena | the treatment under test (required by the question) |\n| **H-C** causal Hyena | \"any Hyena would do; bidirectionality is irrelevant\" |\n| **H-noL** Hyena minus the long conv (gating + short conv only) | \"it's the gated block/stack, not the long kernel\" |\n| **S0±** attention matched on **params AND FLOPs** | \"you just resized the baseline\" |\n| **S0-rec** sliding-window attention with context = Hyena receptive field | \"it's only effective context length\" |\n| **R-floor** copy-last-state + phase-randomized surrogate | gives the metric a meaningful bottom; catches \"smooth blur wins\" |\n| **R-ceiling** analytic GT rollout + GT-noise reference | calibrates the noise floor so ê(t) is interpretable |\nThis set alone supports the claim **\"in this architecture and task, the non-causal long-kernel operator (not capacity, not context, not causality) drives long-horizon consistency.\"**\n\n**OPTIONAL (ablation-grade) — one line each: rival explanation / loss if omitted:**\n- **O1 objective factor** (single-step/short-window training only): closes \"the multi-step objective did it, not the operator\" / if omitted, training-objective confound is uncontrolled — **highest-priority optional**.\n- **O2 global SSM (S4/LTU-style):** closes \"any global linear-recurrence class would do\" / if omitted, family-level claims unsupported (claim stays operator-level).\n- **O3 LSTM/GRU:** closes \"recurrent memory alone handles long horizons\" / if omitted, no non-attention/non-conv reference point.\n- **O4 ALiBi/RoPE-length-extrapolated attention at matched FLOPs:** closes \"standard long-context positional tricks already suffice (strawman baseline)\" / if omitted, the attention anchor is attackable.\n- **O5 Hyena kernel-decay sweep** (poly α ∈ {0.5,1,1.5,2}, exp, learned): closes \"one lucky kernel hyperparameter\" / if omitted, effect size may be hyperparameter luck.\n- **O6 iso-FLOPs width/depth sweep for both families:** closes \"parity was tuned at a single operating point\" / if omitted, capacity parity is a point estimate.\n\n**Run grid:** mandatory 6 trained arms × 5 seeds = **30**; long-horizon-finetune factor (train-only vs long-finetuned) on {S0, H-NC, H-C} = **+15**; O1 objective factor on {S0, H-NC} = **+10** → **55 trained runs** for the confirmatory core (down from 90 in the first pass); M1/M2/M3 differ only in inference, so evaluation adds sampling cost, not training cost; O2–O6 ≈ +10–25 runs if compute permits.\n\n## 6. Protocol\nTraining: interpolant/diffusion objective on windows of W_train with prefix-mixup conditioning; \"long-horizon finetuning\" is a **separate crossed factor** (never folded into an arm), because horizon extrapolation is a known curriculum artifact. Evaluation beyond W_train uses: exact/two-solver GT rollouts from the same IC, invariant and self-consistency drift, and ensemble distributional statistics. **5 seeds/arm**, median as the primary statistic, **paired by seed and by IC**; identical batch order and noise streams across paired arms; all seeds plotted. Metric code and analysis spec are frozen and hash-logged before any run.\n\n## 7. Pre-registered success / failure criteria (our values, not the paper's)\n- **C1 existence:** median H-NC beats S0 on M2 ALOHE by **≥30%** at W = 16 W_train, paired-bootstrap 95% CI (10⁴ resamples) excludes 0.\n- **C2 timescale (definitional for H1-slow):** τ_slow relative recovery-error improvement **≥30%** AND slow-band spectral cosine **≥0.8**; fast-only gain ⇒ **not confirmed** (see §2).\n- **C3 attribution:** H-C loses to H-NC by ≥20% on the slow slice **and** H-noL loses by ≥20%; if |S0± − H-NC| < 10% the effect is attributed to capacity ⇒ H1-rejected-as-operator-claim; if |S0-rec − H-NC| < 10% it is attributed to context length ⇒ same verdict.\n- **C4 compositional transfer:** M3 ordering (H-NC > S0 in ALOHE-AR and a smaller compounding exponent). If M2 passes and M3 fails, the verdict is explicitly **\"long-range representation yes / generated long trajectories via chaining no\"** — a partial, pre-named outcome.\n- **C5 repeatability:** ≥4/5 seeds individually clear the bar, consistent sign across seeds; if inter-seed spread exceeds the effect, the result is declared **inconclusive**, not averaged away.\n- **C6 control sanity:** D3 shows no arm separating from R-floor beyond the chaos ceiling; violation ⇒ harness audit before any conclusion.\nDecision table pre-registers exactly four labels: **supported (operator-level, both modes)** / **supported for representation only (C4 fails)** / **attributed to a confound (C3 fails)** / **unsupported**.\n\n## 8. Analysis plan\nPrimary estimand: median-over-seeds ALOHE and slow-slice metrics, paired bootstrap, Holm correction over the secondary metric family. Slices: horizon W ∈ {1,2,4,8,16,32}×W_train × timescale slice (fast/slow) × ρ ∈ {10,10²,10³} × regime × train-only/long-finetuned. **Length-frontier analysis** (the main figure): for each arm, the largest W at which slow-band cosine ≥ 0.8 — chosen deliberately because it stays well-defined when arms have different computable-length ceilings. **Length-ceiling honesty rule:** if bidirectional attention cannot even *evaluate* at 16 W_train (O(n²) memory), that is reported as a documented constraint with the maximum evaluated length per arm; the comparison is then made on the shared frontier, so \"OOM\" never silently counts as a win. Error decomposition into bias (drift) / variance / misplaced spectral power; per-decade error curves. **Main confound = training objective/curriculum**, closed by the arm × objective × finetune factorial and a pre-registered interaction test; secondary confounds closed by S0±, S0-rec, R-floor/R-ceiling, analytic GT in D1, dual solvers in D2. Seed count is fixed by a pre-registered 2-seed pilot on D1 to estimate σ before the confirmatory grid.\n\n## 9. Feasibility, and one blocking implementation finding\nFeasible **in this environment, stdlib-only, CPU** (already demonstrated as implementation checks, not as experiments): pure-Python long convolution via FFT at n = 65 536 in 1.5 s and n = 131 072 in 3.2 s; direct convolution n = 4096, kernel 1024 in 0.42 s; FFT-vs-direct agreement 1.3e-15 / 1.9e-15; symmetric-kernel error 0.0; kernel length 2L−1 as designed. So the operator unit-check suite (kernel symmetry, receptive-field length, FFT-vs-direct equivalence, O(n log n) scaling, causal/non-causal mask correctness) is runnable here at evaluation-relevant lengths.\n\n**Blocking pre-flight test — \"non-causal\" must be tested as support, not as shape.** Our check showed that a symmetric-shape kernel applied with *right-aligned* convolution is still **strictly causal** (influence of a future input on earlier outputs = 0.000e+00), whereas the *center-aligned* application is genuinely non-causal (3.54e-01). A naive \"flip-and-concat + standard conv\" implementation therefore silently turns the mandatory arm into a causal one and collapses the entire attribution chain. Additionally, edge truncation is asymmetric (left-edge impulse: energy 2.12 left-of-centre vs 0.13 right), so the boundary policy (zero-pad / reflect / crop) must be declared and held identical across arms. Gate: **H-NC is admitted to the grid only after passing an influence-function test, recorded in the pre-flight log.**\n\nNot feasible here: any training (no torch, no GPU, no data, no installs), hence all arm-level numbers below are predictions: **P1** H-NC > S0 on ALOHE at large W; **P2** H-NC > H-C specifically in the slow slice; **P3** H-noL ≈ S0-style degradation (long kernel necessary); **P4** no reliable advantage at ρ = 10 (nothing to gain when scales are not separated) — this is a *falsification* prediction: a ρ = 10 win would indicate a capacity or smoothing artifact; **P5** gains shift toward Hyena as W grows but both families degrade in D3.\n\n## 10. Assumptions (mine, not fixed by the brief or the source)\nW_train = 1024; \"extreme\" = 16× (up to 32× by chaining); domain = my synthetic/analytic family D1–D4, primary D1; d ∈ {2…16} low-dim modality (my decision per your edit 1) ⇒ perceptual metrics deleted; P = 128 GT prefix for M2; Δ = W_train/2 for M3; d_model 512, depth 8, N ≈ 10–25 M params; ≈ 2–5·10⁹ training tokens per run ⇒ ≈ 30–130 GPU-hours/run and ≈ 2–7·10³ GPU-hours for the 55-run core (formula-based estimate, unverifiable here); 5 seeds; Hyena = gated long depthwise conv with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, non-causal = center-aligned symmetric kernel; all numeric thresholds (30%, 20%, 10%, 3σ, 0.8, 4/5 seeds) are **our pre-registration values, not reproductions**; exact/two-solver GT rollouts available at any horizon; original SiT attention spec (bidirectional, head/depth, positional encoding) reconstructed from general knowledge since the source is absent.\n\n## 11. Open items for you\nWhether the interpolant sampler/schedule and step count are treated as fixed hyperparameters across arms (I propose fixed, arm-independent, and I have assumed so); whether D4 enters the confirmatory grid or the extension set (I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count); and whether you want O1 promoted to mandatory if compute allows (it is the single most load-bearing optional control).", "evidence": "ENVIRONMENT / REPO OBSERVATIONS (exploration, not experiment outcomes): ls -la /workspace and find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -> only task.json (511 B); cat task.json -> \"datasets\": [] and documents.track.md as a string only (find -name track.md finds no file); python3 3.14.4; import numpy/torch -> ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no numpy/torch/scipy; urllib to pypi.org -> \"Temporary failure in name resolution\"; pip download numpy fails; nvidia-smi -> cannot communicate with NVIDIA driver (CUDA 13.1 toolkit files present, no driver); nproc=224, RAM ~2011 GB; find -iname '*hyena*'/'*sit*' -> no project code; no *.md outside system paths -> no source paper. So no SiT, Hyena, data, configs or metrics exist; nothing was trained and no arm-level results are claimed.\n\nSTDONLY OPERATOR FEASIBILITY CHECKS actually executed (CPU, pure Python; implementation verification, not experiments): (a) FFT vs direct convolution max-abs disagreement 1.33e-15 (n=256, kernel 127) and 1.89e-15 (n=1024, kernel 511) -> FFT long-conv path is numerically equivalent and checkable here; (b) symmetric-kernel asymmetry error 0.00e+00 and kernel length 65 == 2L-1 for L=33 -> receptive-field/symmetry checks are implementable; (c) timing: pure-Python FFT long conv n=65536 in 1.5 s, n=131072 in 3.2 s, direct conv n=4096/L=1024 in 0.42 s -> unit checks at evaluation-relevant sequence lengths (up to ~1.3e5) run in seconds-to-minutes on CPU, so the feasibility block is grounded rather than asserted.\n\nCRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION FINDING driving a blocking gate: with an identical symmetric-shape polynomial-decay kernel, right-aligned convolution gave \"influence of input[t=255] on outputs t<255\" = 0.000e+00 (strictly CAUSAL), while center-aligned convolution gave 3.536e-01 (genuinely NON-CAUSAL). Hence symmetry of the kernel is not evidence of non-causality; a flip-and-concat + standard-conv implementation would silently produce a causal arm and invalidate the H-NC vs H-C attribution. Edge truncation asymmetry also measured: impulse at the left edge produced energy 2.120 left-of-centre vs 0.133 right, which is why the boundary policy must be declared and held equal across arms. These checks motivated the pre-influence-function admission test and the boundary-policy requirement in the design.\n\nDESIGN-COST ARITHMETIC: original plan 9 arms x 2 factors x 5 seeds = 90 runs; revised mandatory set = 6 trained arms x 5 seeds = 30, plus finetune factor on 3 arms = +15, plus O1 objective factor on 2 arms = +10 -> 55 confirmatory trained runs, with M1/M2/M3 sharing checkpoints (inference-only cost), matching the researcher's request for a minimal sufficient attribution set.", "assumptions": ["W_train = 1024 steps and 'extremely long' = 16x W_train (16384), with chaining probing 32x; none of these are specified in the brief", "Primary evaluation mode M2 uses a 128-step ground-truth prefix and a single-shot continuation; this conditioning mechanism is my design choice, not a source detail", "Modality is low-dimensional state (d = 2..16) and therefore perceptual metrics are excluded entirely - a decision taken per the researcher's instruction, not derived from a source", "Primary domain D1 is a linear two-timescale stochastic oscillator with exact matrix-power ground truth; specific systems, noise levels and rho = {10, 100, 1000} are my choices", "Model scale d_model 512, depth 8, N ~ 10-25M params, 2-5e9 training tokens, ~30-130 GPU-hours per run and ~2-7e3 GPU-hours for the 55-run core: formula-based estimates that cannot be measured in this environment", "5 seeds per arm, 2-seed variance pilot before the confirmatory grid; seed count is my pre-registration choice", "Hyena is implemented as gated long depthwise convolution with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, with the non-causal variant realized as a center-aligned symmetric kernel; exact source kernel form is unknown", "All thresholds (30% ALOHE gain, 20%/10% attribution margins, 3-sigma tube, 0.8 slow-band cosine, 4/5 seed consistency) are this design's pre-registration values, explicitly not reproductions of any paper's numbers", "Original SiT attention configuration (bidirectional attention, heads, depth, positional encoding) is reconstructed from general knowledge because the source is not available in the environment", "Exact or dual-solver ground-truth rollouts are available at arbitrary horizons for the chosen simulators"], "uncertainties": ["Whether the interpolant sampler type/step count should be held identical across arms (assumed yes); if the source used arm-specific sampling, matched-budget accounting changes", "Whether M3 (autoregressive chaining) should be a full arm x scheme factorial from the start rather than a contingency on the 3 attribution-critical arms", "Whether D4 (slow-mode-rich extended system) belongs in the confirmatory grid or the extension set; I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count", "Whether O1 (single-step objective factor) is promoted to mandatory, which would raise the confirmatory core to 6 trained-arm families and is the most load-bearing optional control", "Bidirectional attention may be memory-bound at 16x W_train; if true, the length-frontier (shared-length) comparison carries the whole length-extrapolation claim, and the conclusion is weaker than a same-length comparison", "Inter-seed variance is unknown before the pilot; if sigma exceeds the effect size the design yields 'inconclusive' rather than a verdict", "Whether the low-dimensional-state conclusion generalizes to higher-dimensional observation spaces; that generalization is explicitly out of scope of this design"], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8d721ad0656e6ea9", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-8d721ad0656e6ea9", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN (design-only)\\n**Question (H1):** does replacing SiT's time attention with a **non-causal Hyena** operator let the model generate extremely long, consistent trajectories that capture dynamics over **multiple timescales**?\\n\\n**Standing declarations.** (1) Nothing was trained; every quantitative statement below about arms is a **prediction**, never a result. (2) All thresholds are **our pre-registration values, fixed before any run \\u2014 not reproduction of paper numbers**; the source paper is not present in this environment, so no anchoring to reported figures is possible. (3) Perceptual metrics are **removed entirely** (primary and secondary) \\u2014 see Modality.\\n\\n---\\n## 1. Environment facts (fixed conditions, not results)\\n`/workspace` contains only `task.json` (511 B): no SiT code, no Hyena implementation/spec, no trajectory datasets (`datasets: []`), no configs, no metric code, no source text. Python 3.14 stdlib-only; numpy/torch/scipy absent; DNS dead and `pip download` fails (deps unobtainable); `nvidia-smi` cannot reach a driver (CUDA toolkit present, no driver); 224 CPUs, ~2 TB RAM. Consequence: all training-scale claims are unexecutable here; the design is validated as a design.\\n\\n## 2. Hypothesis, operationalized (incl. your edit 3)\\n**Timescales are a property of the TASK, not of the model.** Each domain is pre-profiled (ACF decay times, eigenvalue moduli / Lyapunov exponents, power spectrum) and must expose two well-separated scales \\u03c4_fast \\u2248 20\\u201350 steps and \\u03c4_slow \\u2248 10\\u00b3\\u201310\\u2074 steps, with ratio \\u03c1 = \\u03c4_slow/\\u03c4_fast swept over {10, 10\\u00b2, 10\\u00b3}. Profiling is published before training; \\\"multi-timescale\\\" is then measured by **timescale-resolved slices** (fast window = 5\\u03c4_fast; slow band = frequency interval [1/(5\\u03c4_slow), 1/\\u03c4_fast]).\\n\\n**H1 is a conjunction, stated up front:**\\n- **H1-length** \\u2014 generated horizon W \\u2265 16 \\u00d7 W_train remains consistent;\\n- **H1-slow** \\u2014 consistency holds in the **slow** slice (not only the fast one);\\n- **H1-attrib** \\u2014 the gain survives the attribution controls (causal / no-long-kernel / capacity / context-length).\\n\\n**A gain confined to the fast slice means H1 is NOT CONFIRMED, by definition of H1-slow** \\u2014 not merely a falsifier in a later section. If H1-length holds but H1-slow fails, the verdict is pre-classified as \\\"short-horizon smoothing only, hypothesis unsupported.\\\"\\n\\n**Horizon:** W_train = 1024 steps (assumption); \\\"extremely long\\\" = 16\\u00d7 = 16 384 (assumption); chaining mode probes 32\\u00d7 = 32 768.\\n\\n## 3. Generation scheme \\u2014 fork resolved (your edit 1)\\nSiT in the original sense is an **interpolant/diffusion-style generative model over a whole object**, not an autoregressive unroller. We adopt **(b) whole-window generation as the primary scheme**, for three reasons: (i) it is the faithful instantiation of SiT; (ii) a **non-causal** operator is only meaningful for an object generated as a whole \\u2014 under strict autoregression, bidirectionality collapses to a boundary effect and the \\\"non-causal\\\" claim becomes untestable; (iii) it lets us separate long-range **representation** from **compounding**, which a single AR curve conflates. Autoregression is retained as a **scheme-transfer test**, not as a co-primary scheme, so no metric ever \\\"hangs\\\" between schemes. One trained checkpoint serves three evaluation modes:\\n\\n- **M1 \\u2014 single-shot window generation** (unconditional / system-parameter-conditioned). No per-step GT alignment exists (output is stochastic) \\u2192 **distributional metrics only**: energy/invariant drift within the window, Wasserstein-1 distance of stationary marginals, **slow-band spectral cosine**, decay-time/\\u03c4 fit error, ensemble diversity (anti-mode-collapse). Supports H1-length and H1-slow claims about the trajectory *as an object*.\\n- **M2 \\u2014 prefix-conditioned ONE-SHOT continuation (PRIMARY ESTIMAND).** The window model is conditioned on a real GT prefix of length P = 128 (the prefix is re-fixed at every denoising/interpolant step; the future region is generated). Because the continuation is produced in a single sampling pass, the error-vs-step curve contains **no autoregressive compounding** \\u2192 it isolates representational long-range structure. Metrics: relative error \\u00ea(t) normalized by the GT-noise floor, **ALOHE** (area under \\u00ea up to failure threshold) at W = 16 W_train, first-exit time from the 3\\u03c3_GT tube, \\u03c4_slow recovery error, slow-band spectral cosine, fast-window curvature RMS.\\n- **M3 \\u2014 iterative/AR chaining (scheme-transfer, secondary).** The same model is re-conditioned every \\u0394 = W_train/2 up to 32 W_train. Metrics: log-error compounding exponent (fitted slope), ALOHE-AR, first-exit, invariant drift. Applied to the three attribution-critical arms (S0, H-NC, H-C) only; if M3 contradicts M2 for H-NC, the arm \\u00d7 scheme factorial is escalated **as a pre-registered contingency**, not silently chosen post hoc.\\n\\n**Modality decision:** primary modality is **low-dimensional observable state, d \\u2208 {2\\u202616}**. Therefore **no perceptual/perceptual-quality metric appears anywhere in this design** (not even as secondary); a high-dimensional/video instantiation is explicitly out of scope, and with it any perceptual metric.\\n\\n## 4. Data / domains\\nDeterministic or exactly-solvable simulators (no network needed, no licensing, reproducible seeds).\\n- **D1 (PRIMARY): linear stochastic 2-timescale oscillator** \\u2014 state transition via a linear propagator with two separated eigenvalue moduli, plus observation noise. GT rollout = **exact matrix powers**, so there is **no integrator-error confound** in the primary domain; \\u03c4_fast, \\u03c4_slow, \\u03c1, noise level are explicit knobs.\\n- **D2 (realism):** damped/driven pendulum + slow parameter drift (nonlinear; GT from two independent solvers, disagreement = GT noise band).\\n- **D3 (positive control, harness leak detector):** fine-step chaotic system (Lorenz/R\\u00f6ssler). Prediction: every arm saturates at the chaos ceiling; **a clean \\\"win\\\" here flags leakage** (GT information, IC overlap, normalization leak) and triggers harness audit.\\n- **D4 (slow-mode rich):** coupled-oscillator lattice / N-body with slow coarsening \\u2014 stresses the slow band.\\n- **D5:** real offline trajectory corpus \\u2014 **not available here** (network off, datasets empty); listed as an extension, not part of the confirmatory grid.\\nSplits are **family-level**: train/val/test disjoint in initial conditions *and* in system parameters; plus a **far-extrapolation** split with parameters outside the training range.\\n\\n## 5. Arms, sorted by necessity (your edit 2)\\nBudget parity: fixed d_model/depth family, **measured** params and FLOPs/token, identical tokens, optimizer, schedules, sampling budget; wall-clock and peak memory reported as part of the budget ledger.\\n\\n**MANDATORY \\u2014 minimal attribution set (6 trained + 2 free references):**\\n| Arm | Rival explanation it closes |\\n|---|---|\\n| **S0** SiT + original full (bidirectional) time attention | \\\"there is nothing to beat\\\" \\u2014 anchor |\\n| **H-NC** SiT + non-causal Hyena | the treatment under test (required by the question) |\\n| **H-C** causal Hyena | \\\"any Hyena would do; bidirectionality is irrelevant\\\" |\\n| **H-noL** Hyena minus the long conv (gating + short conv only) | \\\"it's the gated block/stack, not the long kernel\\\" |\\n| **S0\\u00b1** attention matched on **params AND FLOPs** | \\\"you just resized the baseline\\\" |\\n| **S0-rec** sliding-window attention with context = Hyena receptive field | \\\"it's only effective context length\\\" |\\n| **R-floor** copy-last-state + phase-randomized surrogate | gives the metric a meaningful bottom; catches \\\"smooth blur wins\\\" |\\n| **R-ceiling** analytic GT rollout + GT-noise reference | calibrates the noise floor so \\u00ea(t) is interpretable |\\nThis set alone supports the claim **\\\"in this architecture and task, the non-causal long-kernel operator (not capacity, not context, not causality) drives long-horizon consistency.\\\"**\\n\\n**OPTIONAL (ablation-grade) \\u2014 one line each: rival explanation / loss if omitted:**\\n- **O1 objective factor** (single-step/short-window training only): closes \\\"the multi-step objective did it, not the operator\\\" / if omitted, training-objective confound is uncontrolled \\u2014 **highest-priority optional**.\\n- **O2 global SSM (S4/LTU-style):** closes \\\"any global linear-recurrence class would do\\\" / if omitted, family-level claims unsupported (claim stays operator-level).\\n- **O3 LSTM/GRU:** closes \\\"recurrent memory alone handles long horizons\\\" / if omitted, no non-attention/non-conv reference point.\\n- **O4 ALiBi/RoPE-length-extrapolated attention at matched FLOPs:** closes \\\"standard long-context positional tricks already suffice (strawman baseline)\\\" / if omitted, the attention anchor is attackable.\\n- **O5 Hyena kernel-decay sweep** (poly \\u03b1 \\u2208 {0.5,1,1.5,2}, exp, learned): closes \\\"one lucky kernel hyperparameter\\\" / if omitted, effect size may be hyperparameter luck.\\n- **O6 iso-FLOPs width/depth sweep for both families:** closes \\\"parity was tuned at a single operating point\\\" / if omitted, capacity parity is a point estimate.\\n\\n**Run grid:** mandatory 6 trained arms \\u00d7 5 seeds = **30**; long-horizon-finetune factor (train-only vs long-finetuned) on {S0, H-NC, H-C} = **+15**; O1 objective factor on {S0, H-NC} = **+10** \\u2192 **55 trained runs** for the confirmatory core (down from 90 in the first pass); M1/M2/M3 differ only in inference, so evaluation adds sampling cost, not training cost; O2\\u2013O6 \\u2248 +10\\u201325 runs if compute permits.\\n\\n## 6. Protocol\\nTraining: interpolant/diffusion objective on windows of W_train with prefix-mixup conditioning; \\\"long-horizon finetuning\\\" is a **separate crossed factor** (never folded into an arm), because horizon extrapolation is a known curriculum artifact. Evaluation beyond W_train uses: exact/two-solver GT rollouts from the same IC, invariant and self-consistency drift, and ensemble distributional statistics. **5 seeds/arm**, median as the primary statistic, **paired by seed and by IC**; identical batch order and noise streams across paired arms; all seeds plotted. Metric code and analysis spec are frozen and hash-logged before any run.\\n\\n## 7. Pre-registered success / failure criteria (our values, not the paper's)\\n- **C1 existence:** median H-NC beats S0 on M2 ALOHE by **\\u226530%** at W = 16 W_train, paired-bootstrap 95% CI (10\\u2074 resamples) excludes 0.\\n- **C2 timescale (definitional for H1-slow):** \\u03c4_slow relative recovery-error improvement **\\u226530%** AND slow-band spectral cosine **\\u22650.8**; fast-only gain \\u21d2 **not confirmed** (see \\u00a72).\\n- **C3 attribution:** H-C loses to H-NC by \\u226520% on the slow slice **and** H-noL loses by \\u226520%; if |S0\\u00b1 \\u2212 H-NC| < 10% the effect is attributed to capacity \\u21d2 H1-rejected-as-operator-claim; if |S0-rec \\u2212 H-NC| < 10% it is attributed to context length \\u21d2 same verdict.\\n- **C4 compositional transfer:** M3 ordering (H-NC > S0 in ALOHE-AR and a smaller compounding exponent). If M2 passes and M3 fails, the verdict is explicitly **\\\"long-range representation yes / generated long trajectories via chaining no\\\"** \\u2014 a partial, pre-named outcome.\\n- **C5 repeatability:** \\u22654/5 seeds individually clear the bar, consistent sign across seeds; if inter-seed spread exceeds the effect, the result is declared **inconclusive**, not averaged away.\\n- **C6 control sanity:** D3 shows no arm separating from R-floor beyond the chaos ceiling; violation \\u21d2 harness audit before any conclusion.\\nDecision table pre-registers exactly four labels: **supported (operator-level, both modes)** / **supported for representation only (C4 fails)** / **attributed to a confound (C3 fails)** / **unsupported**.\\n\\n## 8. Analysis plan\\nPrimary estimand: median-over-seeds ALOHE and slow-slice metrics, paired bootstrap, Holm correction over the secondary metric family. Slices: horizon W \\u2208 {1,2,4,8,16,32}\\u00d7W_train \\u00d7 timescale slice (fast/slow) \\u00d7 \\u03c1 \\u2208 {10,10\\u00b2,10\\u00b3} \\u00d7 regime \\u00d7 train-only/long-finetuned. **Length-frontier analysis** (the main figure): for each arm, the largest W at which slow-band cosine \\u2265 0.8 \\u2014 chosen deliberately because it stays well-defined when arms have different computable-length ceilings. **Length-ceiling honesty rule:** if bidirectional attention cannot even *evaluate* at 16 W_train (O(n\\u00b2) memory), that is reported as a documented constraint with the maximum evaluated length per arm; the comparison is then made on the shared frontier, so \\\"OOM\\\" never silently counts as a win. Error decomposition into bias (drift) / variance / misplaced spectral power; per-decade error curves. **Main confound = training objective/curriculum**, closed by the arm \\u00d7 objective \\u00d7 finetune factorial and a pre-registered interaction test; secondary confounds closed by S0\\u00b1, S0-rec, R-floor/R-ceiling, analytic GT in D1, dual solvers in D2. Seed count is fixed by a pre-registered 2-seed pilot on D1 to estimate \\u03c3 before the confirmatory grid.\\n\\n## 9. Feasibility, and one blocking implementation finding\\nFeasible **in this environment, stdlib-only, CPU** (already demonstrated as implementation checks, not as experiments): pure-Python long convolution via FFT at n = 65 536 in 1.5 s and n = 131 072 in 3.2 s; direct convolution n = 4096, kernel 1024 in 0.42 s; FFT-vs-direct agreement 1.3e-15 / 1.9e-15; symmetric-kernel error 0.0; kernel length 2L\\u22121 as designed. So the operator unit-check suite (kernel symmetry, receptive-field length, FFT-vs-direct equivalence, O(n log n) scaling, causal/non-causal mask correctness) is runnable here at evaluation-relevant lengths.\\n\\n**Blocking pre-flight test \\u2014 \\\"non-causal\\\" must be tested as support, not as shape.** Our check showed that a symmetric-shape kernel applied with *right-aligned* convolution is still **strictly causal** (influence of a future input on earlier outputs = 0.000e+00), whereas the *center-aligned* application is genuinely non-causal (3.54e-01). A naive \\\"flip-and-concat + standard conv\\\" implementation therefore silently turns the mandatory arm into a causal one and collapses the entire attribution chain. Additionally, edge truncation is asymmetric (left-edge impulse: energy 2.12 left-of-centre vs 0.13 right), so the boundary policy (zero-pad / reflect / crop) must be declared and held identical across arms. Gate: **H-NC is admitted to the grid only after passing an influence-function test, recorded in the pre-flight log.**\\n\\nNot feasible here: any training (no torch, no GPU, no data, no installs), hence all arm-level numbers below are predictions: **P1** H-NC > S0 on ALOHE at large W; **P2** H-NC > H-C specifically in the slow slice; **P3** H-noL \\u2248 S0-style degradation (long kernel necessary); **P4** no reliable advantage at \\u03c1 = 10 (nothing to gain when scales are not separated) \\u2014 this is a *falsification* prediction: a \\u03c1 = 10 win would indicate a capacity or smoothing artifact; **P5** gains shift toward Hyena as W grows but both families degrade in D3.\\n\\n## 10. Assumptions (mine, not fixed by the brief or the source)\\nW_train = 1024; \\\"extreme\\\" = 16\\u00d7 (up to 32\\u00d7 by chaining); domain = my synthetic/analytic family D1\\u2013D4, primary D1; d \\u2208 {2\\u202616} low-dim modality (my decision per your edit 1) \\u21d2 perceptual metrics deleted; P = 128 GT prefix for M2; \\u0394 = W_train/2 for M3; d_model 512, depth 8, N \\u2248 10\\u201325 M params; \\u2248 2\\u20135\\u00b710\\u2079 training tokens per run \\u21d2 \\u2248 30\\u2013130 GPU-hours/run and \\u2248 2\\u20137\\u00b710\\u00b3 GPU-hours for the 55-run core (formula-based estimate, unverifiable here); 5 seeds; Hyena = gated long depthwise conv with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, non-causal = center-aligned symmetric kernel; all numeric thresholds (30%, 20%, 10%, 3\\u03c3, 0.8, 4/5 seeds) are **our pre-registration values, not reproductions**; exact/two-solver GT rollouts available at any horizon; original SiT attention spec (bidirectional, head/depth, positional encoding) reconstructed from general knowledge since the source is absent.\\n\\n## 11. Open items for you\\nWhether the interpolant sampler/schedule and step count are treated as fixed hyperparameters across arms (I propose fixed, arm-independent, and I have assumed so); whether D4 enters the confirmatory grid or the extension set (I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count); and whether you want O1 promoted to mandatory if compute allows (it is the single most load-bearing optional control).\", \"evidence\": \"ENVIRONMENT / REPO OBSERVATIONS (exploration, not experiment outcomes): ls -la /workspace and find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -> only task.json (511 B); cat task.json -> \\\"datasets\\\": [] and documents.track.md as a string only (find -name track.md finds no file); python3 3.14.4; import numpy/torch -> ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no numpy/torch/scipy; urllib to pypi.org -> \\\"Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"; pip download numpy fails; nvidia-smi -> cannot communicate with NVIDIA driver (CUDA 13.1 toolkit files present, no driver); nproc=224, RAM ~2011 GB; find -iname '*hyena*'/'*sit*' -> no project code; no *.md outside system paths -> no source paper. So no SiT, Hyena, data, configs or metrics exist; nothing was trained and no arm-level results are claimed.\\n\\nSTDONLY OPERATOR FEASIBILITY CHECKS actually executed (CPU, pure Python; implementation verification, not experiments): (a) FFT vs direct convolution max-abs disagreement 1.33e-15 (n=256, kernel 127) and 1.89e-15 (n=1024, kernel 511) -> FFT long-conv path is numerically equivalent and checkable here; (b) symmetric-kernel asymmetry error 0.00e+00 and kernel length 65 == 2L-1 for L=33 -> receptive-field/symmetry checks are implementable; (c) timing: pure-Python FFT long conv n=65536 in 1.5 s, n=131072 in 3.2 s, direct conv n=4096/L=1024 in 0.42 s -> unit checks at evaluation-relevant sequence lengths (up to ~1.3e5) run in seconds-to-minutes on CPU, so the feasibility block is grounded rather than asserted.\\n\\nCRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION FINDING driving a blocking gate: with an identical symmetric-shape polynomial-decay kernel, right-aligned convolution gave \\\"influence of input[t=255] on outputs t<255\\\" = 0.000e+00 (strictly CAUSAL), while center-aligned convolution gave 3.536e-01 (genuinely NON-CAUSAL). Hence symmetry of the kernel is not evidence of non-causality; a flip-and-concat + standard-conv implementation would silently produce a causal arm and invalidate the H-NC vs H-C attribution. Edge truncation asymmetry also measured: impulse at the left edge produced energy 2.120 left-of-centre vs 0.133 right, which is why the boundary policy must be declared and held equal across arms. These checks motivated the pre-influence-function admission test and the boundary-policy requirement in the design.\\n\\nDESIGN-COST ARITHMETIC: original plan 9 arms x 2 factors x 5 seeds = 90 runs; revised mandatory set = 6 trained arms x 5 seeds = 30, plus finetune factor on 3 arms = +15, plus O1 objective factor on 2 arms = +10 -> 55 confirmatory trained runs, with M1/M2/M3 sharing checkpoints (inference-only cost), matching the researcher's request for a minimal sufficient attribution set.\", \"assumptions\": [\"W_train = 1024 steps and 'extremely long' = 16x W_train (16384), with chaining probing 32x; none of these are specified in the brief\", \"Primary evaluation mode M2 uses a 128-step ground-truth prefix and a single-shot continuation; this conditioning mechanism is my design choice, not a source detail\", \"Modality is low-dimensional state (d = 2..16) and therefore perceptual metrics are excluded entirely - a decision taken per the researcher's instruction, not derived from a source\", \"Primary domain D1 is a linear two-timescale stochastic oscillator with exact matrix-power ground truth; specific systems, noise levels and rho = {10, 100, 1000} are my choices\", \"Model scale d_model 512, depth 8, N ~ 10-25M params, 2-5e9 training tokens, ~30-130 GPU-hours per run and ~2-7e3 GPU-hours for the 55-run core: formula-based estimates that cannot be measured in this environment\", \"5 seeds per arm, 2-seed variance pilot before the confirmatory grid; seed count is my pre-registration choice\", \"Hyena is implemented as gated long depthwise convolution with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, with the non-causal variant realized as a center-aligned symmetric kernel; exact source kernel form is unknown\", \"All thresholds (30% ALOHE gain, 20%/10% attribution margins, 3-sigma tube, 0.8 slow-band cosine, 4/5 seed consistency) are this design's pre-registration values, explicitly not reproductions of any paper's numbers\", \"Original SiT attention configuration (bidirectional attention, heads, depth, positional encoding) is reconstructed from general knowledge because the source is not available in the environment\", \"Exact or dual-solver ground-truth rollouts are available at arbitrary horizons for the chosen simulators\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the interpolant sampler type/step count should be held identical across arms (assumed yes); if the source used arm-specific sampling, matched-budget accounting changes\", \"Whether M3 (autoregressive chaining) should be a full arm x scheme factorial from the start rather than a contingency on the 3 attribution-critical arms\", \"Whether D4 (slow-mode-rich extended system) belongs in the confirmatory grid or the extension set; I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count\", \"Whether O1 (single-step objective factor) is promoted to mandatory, which would raise the confirmatory core to 6 trained-arm families and is the most load-bearing optional control\", \"Bidirectional attention may be memory-bound at 16x W_train; if true, the length-frontier (shared-length) comparison carries the whole length-extrapolation claim, and the conclusion is weaker than a same-length comparison\", \"Inter-seed variance is unknown before the pilot; if sigma exceeds the effect size the design yields 'inconclusive' rather than a verdict\", \"Whether the low-dimensional-state conclusion generalizes to higher-dimensional observation spaces; that generalization is explicitly out of scope of this design\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-30246d21-5e6d-4500-8b8d-684a071093f5", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN (design-only)\\n**Question (H1):** does replacing SiT's time attention with a **non-causal Hyena** operator let the model generate extremely long, consistent trajectories that capture dynamics over **multiple timescales**?\\n\\n**Standing declarations.** (1) Nothing was trained; every quantitative statement below about arms is a **prediction**, never a result. (2) All thresholds are **our pre-registration values, fixed before any run \\u2014 not reproduction of paper numbers**; the source paper is not present in this environment, so no anchoring to reported figures is possible. (3) Perceptual metrics are **removed entirely** (primary and secondary) \\u2014 see Modality.\\n\\n---\\n## 1. Environment facts (fixed conditions, not results)\\n`/workspace` contains only `task.json` (511 B): no SiT code, no Hyena implementation/spec, no trajectory datasets (`datasets: []`), no configs, no metric code, no source text. Python 3.14 stdlib-only; numpy/torch/scipy absent; DNS dead and `pip download` fails (deps unobtainable); `nvidia-smi` cannot reach a driver (CUDA toolkit present, no driver); 224 CPUs, ~2 TB RAM. Consequence: all training-scale claims are unexecutable here; the design is validated as a design.\\n\\n## 2. Hypothesis, operationalized (incl. your edit 3)\\n**Timescales are a property of the TASK, not of the model.** Each domain is pre-profiled (ACF decay times, eigenvalue moduli / Lyapunov exponents, power spectrum) and must expose two well-separated scales \\u03c4_fast \\u2248 20\\u201350 steps and \\u03c4_slow \\u2248 10\\u00b3\\u201310\\u2074 steps, with ratio \\u03c1 = \\u03c4_slow/\\u03c4_fast swept over {10, 10\\u00b2, 10\\u00b3}. Profiling is published before training; \\\"multi-timescale\\\" is then measured by **timescale-resolved slices** (fast window = 5\\u03c4_fast; slow band = frequency interval [1/(5\\u03c4_slow), 1/\\u03c4_fast]).\\n\\n**H1 is a conjunction, stated up front:**\\n- **H1-length** \\u2014 generated horizon W \\u2265 16 \\u00d7 W_train remains consistent;\\n- **H1-slow** \\u2014 consistency holds in the **slow** slice (not only the fast one);\\n- **H1-attrib** \\u2014 the gain survives the attribution controls (causal / no-long-kernel / capacity / context-length).\\n\\n**A gain confined to the fast slice means H1 is NOT CONFIRMED, by definition of H1-slow** \\u2014 not merely a falsifier in a later section. If H1-length holds but H1-slow fails, the verdict is pre-classified as \\\"short-horizon smoothing only, hypothesis unsupported.\\\"\\n\\n**Horizon:** W_train = 1024 steps (assumption); \\\"extremely long\\\" = 16\\u00d7 = 16 384 (assumption); chaining mode probes 32\\u00d7 = 32 768.\\n\\n## 3. Generation scheme \\u2014 fork resolved (your edit 1)\\nSiT in the original sense is an **interpolant/diffusion-style generative model over a whole object**, not an autoregressive unroller. We adopt **(b) whole-window generation as the primary scheme**, for three reasons: (i) it is the faithful instantiation of SiT; (ii) a **non-causal** operator is only meaningful for an object generated as a whole \\u2014 under strict autoregression, bidirectionality collapses to a boundary effect and the \\\"non-causal\\\" claim becomes untestable; (iii) it lets us separate long-range **representation** from **compounding**, which a single AR curve conflates. Autoregression is retained as a **scheme-transfer test**, not as a co-primary scheme, so no metric ever \\\"hangs\\\" between schemes. One trained checkpoint serves three evaluation modes:\\n\\n- **M1 \\u2014 single-shot window generation** (unconditional / system-parameter-conditioned). No per-step GT alignment exists (output is stochastic) \\u2192 **distributional metrics only**: energy/invariant drift within the window, Wasserstein-1 distance of stationary marginals, **slow-band spectral cosine**, decay-time/\\u03c4 fit error, ensemble diversity (anti-mode-collapse). Supports H1-length and H1-slow claims about the trajectory *as an object*.\\n- **M2 \\u2014 prefix-conditioned ONE-SHOT continuation (PRIMARY ESTIMAND).** The window model is conditioned on a real GT prefix of length P = 128 (the prefix is re-fixed at every denoising/interpolant step; the future region is generated). Because the continuation is produced in a single sampling pass, the error-vs-step curve contains **no autoregressive compounding** \\u2192 it isolates representational long-range structure. Metrics: relative error \\u00ea(t) normalized by the GT-noise floor, **ALOHE** (area under \\u00ea up to failure threshold) at W = 16 W_train, first-exit time from the 3\\u03c3_GT tube, \\u03c4_slow recovery error, slow-band spectral cosine, fast-window curvature RMS.\\n- **M3 \\u2014 iterative/AR chaining (scheme-transfer, secondary).** The same model is re-conditioned every \\u0394 = W_train/2 up to 32 W_train. Metrics: log-error compounding exponent (fitted slope), ALOHE-AR, first-exit, invariant drift. Applied to the three attribution-critical arms (S0, H-NC, H-C) only; if M3 contradicts M2 for H-NC, the arm \\u00d7 scheme factorial is escalated **as a pre-registered contingency**, not silently chosen post hoc.\\n\\n**Modality decision:** primary modality is **low-dimensional observable state, d \\u2208 {2\\u202616}**. Therefore **no perceptual/perceptual-quality metric appears anywhere in this design** (not even as secondary); a high-dimensional/video instantiation is explicitly out of scope, and with it any perceptual metric.\\n\\n## 4. Data / domains\\nDeterministic or exactly-solvable simulators (no network needed, no licensing, reproducible seeds).\\n- **D1 (PRIMARY): linear stochastic 2-timescale oscillator** \\u2014 state transition via a linear propagator with two separated eigenvalue moduli, plus observation noise. GT rollout = **exact matrix powers**, so there is **no integrator-error confound** in the primary domain; \\u03c4_fast, \\u03c4_slow, \\u03c1, noise level are explicit knobs.\\n- **D2 (realism):** damped/driven pendulum + slow parameter drift (nonlinear; GT from two independent solvers, disagreement = GT noise band).\\n- **D3 (positive control, harness leak detector):** fine-step chaotic system (Lorenz/R\\u00f6ssler). Prediction: every arm saturates at the chaos ceiling; **a clean \\\"win\\\" here flags leakage** (GT information, IC overlap, normalization leak) and triggers harness audit.\\n- **D4 (slow-mode rich):** coupled-oscillator lattice / N-body with slow coarsening \\u2014 stresses the slow band.\\n- **D5:** real offline trajectory corpus \\u2014 **not available here** (network off, datasets empty); listed as an extension, not part of the confirmatory grid.\\nSplits are **family-level**: train/val/test disjoint in initial conditions *and* in system parameters; plus a **far-extrapolation** split with parameters outside the training range.\\n\\n## 5. Arms, sorted by necessity (your edit 2)\\nBudget parity: fixed d_model/depth family, **measured** params and FLOPs/token, identical tokens, optimizer, schedules, sampling budget; wall-clock and peak memory reported as part of the budget ledger.\\n\\n**MANDATORY \\u2014 minimal attribution set (6 trained + 2 free references):**\\n| Arm | Rival explanation it closes |\\n|---|---|\\n| **S0** SiT + original full (bidirectional) time attention | \\\"there is nothing to beat\\\" \\u2014 anchor |\\n| **H-NC** SiT + non-causal Hyena | the treatment under test (required by the question) |\\n| **H-C** causal Hyena | \\\"any Hyena would do; bidirectionality is irrelevant\\\" |\\n| **H-noL** Hyena minus the long conv (gating + short conv only) | \\\"it's the gated block/stack, not the long kernel\\\" |\\n| **S0\\u00b1** attention matched on **params AND FLOPs** | \\\"you just resized the baseline\\\" |\\n| **S0-rec** sliding-window attention with context = Hyena receptive field | \\\"it's only effective context length\\\" |\\n| **R-floor** copy-last-state + phase-randomized surrogate | gives the metric a meaningful bottom; catches \\\"smooth blur wins\\\" |\\n| **R-ceiling** analytic GT rollout + GT-noise reference | calibrates the noise floor so \\u00ea(t) is interpretable |\\nThis set alone supports the claim **\\\"in this architecture and task, the non-causal long-kernel operator (not capacity, not context, not causality) drives long-horizon consistency.\\\"**\\n\\n**OPTIONAL (ablation-grade) \\u2014 one line each: rival explanation / loss if omitted:**\\n- **O1 objective factor** (single-step/short-window training only): closes \\\"the multi-step objective did it, not the operator\\\" / if omitted, training-objective confound is uncontrolled \\u2014 **highest-priority optional**.\\n- **O2 global SSM (S4/LTU-style):** closes \\\"any global linear-recurrence class would do\\\" / if omitted, family-level claims unsupported (claim stays operator-level).\\n- **O3 LSTM/GRU:** closes \\\"recurrent memory alone handles long horizons\\\" / if omitted, no non-attention/non-conv reference point.\\n- **O4 ALiBi/RoPE-length-extrapolated attention at matched FLOPs:** closes \\\"standard long-context positional tricks already suffice (strawman baseline)\\\" / if omitted, the attention anchor is attackable.\\n- **O5 Hyena kernel-decay sweep** (poly \\u03b1 \\u2208 {0.5,1,1.5,2}, exp, learned): closes \\\"one lucky kernel hyperparameter\\\" / if omitted, effect size may be hyperparameter luck.\\n- **O6 iso-FLOPs width/depth sweep for both families:** closes \\\"parity was tuned at a single operating point\\\" / if omitted, capacity parity is a point estimate.\\n\\n**Run grid:** mandatory 6 trained arms \\u00d7 5 seeds = **30**; long-horizon-finetune factor (train-only vs long-finetuned) on {S0, H-NC, H-C} = **+15**; O1 objective factor on {S0, H-NC} = **+10** \\u2192 **55 trained runs** for the confirmatory core (down from 90 in the first pass); M1/M2/M3 differ only in inference, so evaluation adds sampling cost, not training cost; O2\\u2013O6 \\u2248 +10\\u201325 runs if compute permits.\\n\\n## 6. Protocol\\nTraining: interpolant/diffusion objective on windows of W_train with prefix-mixup conditioning; \\\"long-horizon finetuning\\\" is a **separate crossed factor** (never folded into an arm), because horizon extrapolation is a known curriculum artifact. Evaluation beyond W_train uses: exact/two-solver GT rollouts from the same IC, invariant and self-consistency drift, and ensemble distributional statistics. **5 seeds/arm**, median as the primary statistic, **paired by seed and by IC**; identical batch order and noise streams across paired arms; all seeds plotted. Metric code and analysis spec are frozen and hash-logged before any run.\\n\\n## 7. Pre-registered success / failure criteria (our values, not the paper's)\\n- **C1 existence:** median H-NC beats S0 on M2 ALOHE by **\\u226530%** at W = 16 W_train, paired-bootstrap 95% CI (10\\u2074 resamples) excludes 0.\\n- **C2 timescale (definitional for H1-slow):** \\u03c4_slow relative recovery-error improvement **\\u226530%** AND slow-band spectral cosine **\\u22650.8**; fast-only gain \\u21d2 **not confirmed** (see \\u00a72).\\n- **C3 attribution:** H-C loses to H-NC by \\u226520% on the slow slice **and** H-noL loses by \\u226520%; if |S0\\u00b1 \\u2212 H-NC| < 10% the effect is attributed to capacity \\u21d2 H1-rejected-as-operator-claim; if |S0-rec \\u2212 H-NC| < 10% it is attributed to context length \\u21d2 same verdict.\\n- **C4 compositional transfer:** M3 ordering (H-NC > S0 in ALOHE-AR and a smaller compounding exponent). If M2 passes and M3 fails, the verdict is explicitly **\\\"long-range representation yes / generated long trajectories via chaining no\\\"** \\u2014 a partial, pre-named outcome.\\n- **C5 repeatability:** \\u22654/5 seeds individually clear the bar, consistent sign across seeds; if inter-seed spread exceeds the effect, the result is declared **inconclusive**, not averaged away.\\n- **C6 control sanity:** D3 shows no arm separating from R-floor beyond the chaos ceiling; violation \\u21d2 harness audit before any conclusion.\\nDecision table pre-registers exactly four labels: **supported (operator-level, both modes)** / **supported for representation only (C4 fails)** / **attributed to a confound (C3 fails)** / **unsupported**.\\n\\n## 8. Analysis plan\\nPrimary estimand: median-over-seeds ALOHE and slow-slice metrics, paired bootstrap, Holm correction over the secondary metric family. Slices: horizon W \\u2208 {1,2,4,8,16,32}\\u00d7W_train \\u00d7 timescale slice (fast/slow) \\u00d7 \\u03c1 \\u2208 {10,10\\u00b2,10\\u00b3} \\u00d7 regime \\u00d7 train-only/long-finetuned. **Length-frontier analysis** (the main figure): for each arm, the largest W at which slow-band cosine \\u2265 0.8 \\u2014 chosen deliberately because it stays well-defined when arms have different computable-length ceilings. **Length-ceiling honesty rule:** if bidirectional attention cannot even *evaluate* at 16 W_train (O(n\\u00b2) memory), that is reported as a documented constraint with the maximum evaluated length per arm; the comparison is then made on the shared frontier, so \\\"OOM\\\" never silently counts as a win. Error decomposition into bias (drift) / variance / misplaced spectral power; per-decade error curves. **Main confound = training objective/curriculum**, closed by the arm \\u00d7 objective \\u00d7 finetune factorial and a pre-registered interaction test; secondary confounds closed by S0\\u00b1, S0-rec, R-floor/R-ceiling, analytic GT in D1, dual solvers in D2. Seed count is fixed by a pre-registered 2-seed pilot on D1 to estimate \\u03c3 before the confirmatory grid.\\n\\n## 9. Feasibility, and one blocking implementation finding\\nFeasible **in this environment, stdlib-only, CPU** (already demonstrated as implementation checks, not as experiments): pure-Python long convolution via FFT at n = 65 536 in 1.5 s and n = 131 072 in 3.2 s; direct convolution n = 4096, kernel 1024 in 0.42 s; FFT-vs-direct agreement 1.3e-15 / 1.9e-15; symmetric-kernel error 0.0; kernel length 2L\\u22121 as designed. So the operator unit-check suite (kernel symmetry, receptive-field length, FFT-vs-direct equivalence, O(n log n) scaling, causal/non-causal mask correctness) is runnable here at evaluation-relevant lengths.\\n\\n**Blocking pre-flight test \\u2014 \\\"non-causal\\\" must be tested as support, not as shape.** Our check showed that a symmetric-shape kernel applied with *right-aligned* convolution is still **strictly causal** (influence of a future input on earlier outputs = 0.000e+00), whereas the *center-aligned* application is genuinely non-causal (3.54e-01). A naive \\\"flip-and-concat + standard conv\\\" implementation therefore silently turns the mandatory arm into a causal one and collapses the entire attribution chain. Additionally, edge truncation is asymmetric (left-edge impulse: energy 2.12 left-of-centre vs 0.13 right), so the boundary policy (zero-pad / reflect / crop) must be declared and held identical across arms. Gate: **H-NC is admitted to the grid only after passing an influence-function test, recorded in the pre-flight log.**\\n\\nNot feasible here: any training (no torch, no GPU, no data, no installs), hence all arm-level numbers below are predictions: **P1** H-NC > S0 on ALOHE at large W; **P2** H-NC > H-C specifically in the slow slice; **P3** H-noL \\u2248 S0-style degradation (long kernel necessary); **P4** no reliable advantage at \\u03c1 = 10 (nothing to gain when scales are not separated) \\u2014 this is a *falsification* prediction: a \\u03c1 = 10 win would indicate a capacity or smoothing artifact; **P5** gains shift toward Hyena as W grows but both families degrade in D3.\\n\\n## 10. Assumptions (mine, not fixed by the brief or the source)\\nW_train = 1024; \\\"extreme\\\" = 16\\u00d7 (up to 32\\u00d7 by chaining); domain = my synthetic/analytic family D1\\u2013D4, primary D1; d \\u2208 {2\\u202616} low-dim modality (my decision per your edit 1) \\u21d2 perceptual metrics deleted; P = 128 GT prefix for M2; \\u0394 = W_train/2 for M3; d_model 512, depth 8, N \\u2248 10\\u201325 M params; \\u2248 2\\u20135\\u00b710\\u2079 training tokens per run \\u21d2 \\u2248 30\\u2013130 GPU-hours/run and \\u2248 2\\u20137\\u00b710\\u00b3 GPU-hours for the 55-run core (formula-based estimate, unverifiable here); 5 seeds; Hyena = gated long depthwise conv with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, non-causal = center-aligned symmetric kernel; all numeric thresholds (30%, 20%, 10%, 3\\u03c3, 0.8, 4/5 seeds) are **our pre-registration values, not reproductions**; exact/two-solver GT rollouts available at any horizon; original SiT attention spec (bidirectional, head/depth, positional encoding) reconstructed from general knowledge since the source is absent.\\n\\n## 11. Open items for you\\nWhether the interpolant sampler/schedule and step count are treated as fixed hyperparameters across arms (I propose fixed, arm-independent, and I have assumed so); whether D4 enters the confirmatory grid or the extension set (I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count); and whether you want O1 promoted to mandatory if compute allows (it is the single most load-bearing optional control).\", \"evidence\": \"ENVIRONMENT / REPO OBSERVATIONS (exploration, not experiment outcomes): ls -la /workspace and find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -> only task.json (511 B); cat task.json -> \\\"datasets\\\": [] and documents.track.md as a string only (find -name track.md finds no file); python3 3.14.4; import numpy/torch -> ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no numpy/torch/scipy; urllib to pypi.org -> \\\"Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"; pip download numpy fails; nvidia-smi -> cannot communicate with NVIDIA driver (CUDA 13.1 toolkit files present, no driver); nproc=224, RAM ~2011 GB; find -iname '*hyena*'/'*sit*' -> no project code; no *.md outside system paths -> no source paper. So no SiT, Hyena, data, configs or metrics exist; nothing was trained and no arm-level results are claimed.\\n\\nSTDONLY OPERATOR FEASIBILITY CHECKS actually executed (CPU, pure Python; implementation verification, not experiments): (a) FFT vs direct convolution max-abs disagreement 1.33e-15 (n=256, kernel 127) and 1.89e-15 (n=1024, kernel 511) -> FFT long-conv path is numerically equivalent and checkable here; (b) symmetric-kernel asymmetry error 0.00e+00 and kernel length 65 == 2L-1 for L=33 -> receptive-field/symmetry checks are implementable; (c) timing: pure-Python FFT long conv n=65536 in 1.5 s, n=131072 in 3.2 s, direct conv n=4096/L=1024 in 0.42 s -> unit checks at evaluation-relevant sequence lengths (up to ~1.3e5) run in seconds-to-minutes on CPU, so the feasibility block is grounded rather than asserted.\\n\\nCRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION FINDING driving a blocking gate: with an identical symmetric-shape polynomial-decay kernel, right-aligned convolution gave \\\"influence of input[t=255] on outputs t<255\\\" = 0.000e+00 (strictly CAUSAL), while center-aligned convolution gave 3.536e-01 (genuinely NON-CAUSAL). Hence symmetry of the kernel is not evidence of non-causality; a flip-and-concat + standard-conv implementation would silently produce a causal arm and invalidate the H-NC vs H-C attribution. Edge truncation asymmetry also measured: impulse at the left edge produced energy 2.120 left-of-centre vs 0.133 right, which is why the boundary policy must be declared and held equal across arms. These checks motivated the pre-influence-function admission test and the boundary-policy requirement in the design.\\n\\nDESIGN-COST ARITHMETIC: original plan 9 arms x 2 factors x 5 seeds = 90 runs; revised mandatory set = 6 trained arms x 5 seeds = 30, plus finetune factor on 3 arms = +15, plus O1 objective factor on 2 arms = +10 -> 55 confirmatory trained runs, with M1/M2/M3 sharing checkpoints (inference-only cost), matching the researcher's request for a minimal sufficient attribution set.\", \"assumptions\": [\"W_train = 1024 steps and 'extremely long' = 16x W_train (16384), with chaining probing 32x; none of these are specified in the brief\", \"Primary evaluation mode M2 uses a 128-step ground-truth prefix and a single-shot continuation; this conditioning mechanism is my design choice, not a source detail\", \"Modality is low-dimensional state (d = 2..16) and therefore perceptual metrics are excluded entirely - a decision taken per the researcher's instruction, not derived from a source\", \"Primary domain D1 is a linear two-timescale stochastic oscillator with exact matrix-power ground truth; specific systems, noise levels and rho = {10, 100, 1000} are my choices\", \"Model scale d_model 512, depth 8, N ~ 10-25M params, 2-5e9 training tokens, ~30-130 GPU-hours per run and ~2-7e3 GPU-hours for the 55-run core: formula-based estimates that cannot be measured in this environment\", \"5 seeds per arm, 2-seed variance pilot before the confirmatory grid; seed count is my pre-registration choice\", \"Hyena is implemented as gated long depthwise convolution with polynomial decay plus short conv and gating, with the non-causal variant realized as a center-aligned symmetric kernel; exact source kernel form is unknown\", \"All thresholds (30% ALOHE gain, 20%/10% attribution margins, 3-sigma tube, 0.8 slow-band cosine, 4/5 seed consistency) are this design's pre-registration values, explicitly not reproductions of any paper's numbers\", \"Original SiT attention configuration (bidirectional attention, heads, depth, positional encoding) is reconstructed from general knowledge because the source is not available in the environment\", \"Exact or dual-solver ground-truth rollouts are available at arbitrary horizons for the chosen simulators\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the interpolant sampler type/step count should be held identical across arms (assumed yes); if the source used arm-specific sampling, matched-budget accounting changes\", \"Whether M3 (autoregressive chaining) should be a full arm x scheme factorial from the start rather than a contingency on the 3 attribution-critical arms\", \"Whether D4 (slow-mode-rich extended system) belongs in the confirmatory grid or the extension set; I placed it in the grid at reduced seed count\", \"Whether O1 (single-step objective factor) is promoted to mandatory, which would raise the confirmatory core to 6 trained-arm families and is the most load-bearing optional control\", \"Bidirectional attention may be memory-bound at 16x W_train; if true, the length-frontier (shared-length) comparison carries the whole length-extrapolation claim, and the conclusion is weaker than a same-length comparison\", \"Inter-seed variance is unknown before the pilot; if sigma exceeds the effect size the design yields 'inconclusive' rather than a verdict\", \"Whether the low-dimensional-state conclusion generalizes to higher-dimensional observation spaces; that generalization is explicitly out of scope of this design\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
